{number: 121}
{title: O for a Thousand Tongues}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
O [C] for a thousand [F] tongues to [C] sing
My [F] great Re-[C] deemer's [G7] praise,
The [C] glories of my [F] God and [C] King,
The [F] triumphs [C] of His [G7] [C] grace!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
My [C] gracious Master [F] and my [C] God,
As-[F] sist me [C] to pro-[G7] claim,
To [C] spread through all the [F] earth a-[C] broad
The [F] honors [C] of Thy [G7] [C] name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Jesus! the name that [F] charms our [C] fears,
That [F] bids our [C] sorrows [G7] cease;
'Tis [C] music in the [F] sinner's [C] ears,
'Tis [F] life, and [C] health, and [G7] [C] peace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
He [C] breaks the pow'r of [F] canceled [C] sin,
He [F] sets the [C] pris'ner [G7] free;
His [C] blood can make the [F] foulest [C] clean,
His [F] blood a-[C] vailed for [G7] [C] me.
{end_of_verse}
